Committed `98e6eec` on `fix/nav-mega-menu`. Summary of exact changes:

**BUG-WEB-002 (ladder numbers overlap text):**
- `Header.tsx:279` — `<span className="rung">` → `<span className="step-rung">`
- `ds-nav.css:119` — `counter-reset:rung` → `counter-reset:step-rung`
- `ds-nav.css:127` — `.ladder .rung` → `.ladder .step-rung`, `counter-increment:rung` → `counter-increment:step-rung`
- `ds-nav.css:132` — `.rung::before` → `.step-rung::before`, `counter(rung)` → `counter(step-rung)`
- /how-i-build `.rung` cards untouched

**BUG-WEB-003 (Small business giant empty intro box):**
- `Header.tsx:331` — added `price-list-group` class to the Small business price-list `.mega-group`
- `ds-nav.css:191` — new rule `.site-head--mega .price-list-group{ grid-column:1/-2 }`
- `ds-nav.css:187` — added `align-self:start` to `.panel-note`

**BUG-WEB-004 (can't switch directly between dropdowns):**
- `Header.tsx:184` — added `lastClickRef` ref
- `Header.tsx:207-216` — `openViaClick` sets the flag + clears after 200ms; `openViaHover` returns early if flag is set. This prevents the hover→click race where hover switches the panel and the click toggles the new one closed.

**Mobile clipping:**
- `ds-nav.css:216-223` — `.mega` gets `height:calc(100vh - var(--do-header-h) - 48px); overflow:hidden`; `.mega-inner` gets `overflow-y:auto; height:100%` so mega content scrolls within the panel instead of being clipped by the site-nav overflow.
